{"name":"Buffy Citrine","hex":"#868929","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"buffy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a buff color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/buffy"},{"term":"citrine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A goldish-yellow colour, like that of a lemon.","A brownish-yellow quartz."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a goldish-yellow colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/citrine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Citrine","blocks":[{"text":"Citrine is a transparent, yellow variety of quartz. Its name is derived from the Latin word citrus, by way of the French citrin or citron (lemon). Citrine is one of the most popular yellow gemstones and has been used since ancient Egyptian times. There is disagreement as to which trace elements are responsible for its color. Not all yellow quartz is considered citrine, such as quartz stained by iron inclusions or coatings. Natural citrine is rare; most commercially available \"citrine\" is produced by heating amethyst or smoky quartz."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Citrine_taillee.jpg/330px-Citrine_taillee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Citrine","wikidata":"Q334719"},{"title":"Buff (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Buff is a light brownish yellow, ochreous colour, typical of buff leather. Buff is a mixture of yellow ochre and white: two parts of white lead and one part of yellow ochre produces a good buff, or white lead may be tinted with French ochre alone."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Chamois-natural.jpg/330px-Chamois-natural.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buff_(colour)","wikidata":"Q2085487"},{"title":"Citrine (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Citrine is a colour, the most common reference for which is certain coloured varieties of quartz which are a medium deep shade of golden yellow. Citrine has been summarized at various times as yellow, greenish-yellow, brownish yellow or orange."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Citrin_cut.jpg/330px-Citrin_cut.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Citrine_(colour)","wikidata":"Q5122822"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Citrine_1_%28Russie%29.jpg/120px-Citrine_1_%28Russie%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Citrine_1_%28Russie%29.jpg/250px-Citrine_1_%28Russie%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Citrine_1_%28Russie%29.jpg/120px-Citrine_1_%28Russie%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACitrine_1_(Russie).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Quartz-60953.jpg/120px-Quartz-60953.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Quartz-60953.jpg/250px-Quartz-60953.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Quartz-60953.jpg/120px-Quartz-60953.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AQuartz-60953.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Tumble-polished_citrine_2.jpg/120px-Tumble-polished_citrine_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Tumble-polished_citr